Name      CFDEC_R16;
PartNo    R16-13;
Date      2026-10-17;
Revision  C;
Designer  Reggie-16;
Company   The Bounceworks;
Assembly  Peripheral board (Peripheral_Board.md);
Location  U2;
Device    g22v10;

/*  Reggie-16 peripheral board, block side of the decode pair: the
 *  tick's two strobes and the CF task file's three, every one the AND
 *  of its register decode with the corresponding bus strobe, all fed
 *  from IODEC_R16's /IOWIN (0x3FC0-0x3FEF; the 0x3FEF ceiling is
 *  enforced upstream).  IODEC_R16's header carries the split
 *  rationale; this device never sees A[15:6].
 *
 *  Offsets below are A[5:0] within the window (Peripheral_Board.md
 *  map, where the block bases are final):
 *      0x08  TMRSTA read   / TMRACK write     (0x3FC8)
 *      0x10-0x17  CF task file, /CS0          (0x3FD0-0x3FD7)
 *  Nothing else in the window strobes.  0x09-0x0B and 0x18-0x1F are
 *  free for a card that decodes them itself (Peripheral_Board.md,
 *  Free words): TMRSTA's unpaired senses, the counter's three ports
 *  and the CF control block produce no strobe at all.
 *
 *  HELD OUTPUTS.  /TMRCAPWR, /TMRLORD and /TMRHIRD reach the counter's
 *  sockets, U5-U8, which the machine leaves empty (Timer_Module.md,
 *  Rejected alternatives: a readable counter); /CS1 reaches IDE 38,
 *  and nothing reads the control block it selects (CF_Module.md,
 *  Register interface).  Each is driven high, inactive, rather than
 *  released: the capture carries the '590s, and a released /G would
 *  float.  Their OLMCs are spare in all but copper.
 *
 *  CS0 is address-level (the card qualifies internally with DIOR/DIOW,
 *  exactly as the 16550 does with its strobes); DIOR and DIOW cover the
 *  task file alone and carry the bus strobe.  The '245 pair's DIR rides
 *  /DIOR and their /OE is grounded (CF_Module.md), so /DIOR is what
 *  puts the card on D: it fires nowhere outside 0x3FD0-0x3FD7.
 *
 *  TICKPEND RESET.  /TMRACKWR also asserts whenever RST is high, and
 *  RST comes in on pin 11.  TICKPEND - U9 section A - has D tied high,
 *  /PRE tied high, and /CLR tied to /TMRACKWR and NOTHING ELSE.
 *  /RST_P reaches U14 and H9.1; RST reaches U3, U14 and H7.2; neither
 *  reaches U9.  Without the reset term the flop powers up undefined
 *  and only a CPU write to TMRACK can clear it: a cold start can come
 *  up with a tick already pending and the first EI takes a spurious
 *  interrupt, before the timer is configured and before the ISR
 *  vector is installed - indistinguishable from a real early tick.
 *
 *  The reset lives in this equation rather than in copper because
 *  /TMRACKWR has exactly ONE consumer - U9 pin 1 - so widening it
 *  cannot have a side effect anywhere else on the board.  Asserting it
 *  through reset holds TICKPEND cleared until the machine is running:
 *  the flop is defined from the first instruction rather than from the
 *  first acknowledge.
 *
 *  Pin 11 is the right home for RST and pin 1 is not: pin 1 is the
 *  strobe-stretch provision's CLK, reserved below.
 *
 *  STROBE-STRETCH PROVISION (CF_Module.md, PIO-0 timing): pin 23's
 *  OLMC is the reserved spare.  If the Stage-1 sweep demands the
 *  two-cycle stretch, it becomes the registered leg - pin 1 then
 *  becomes CLK instead of a grounded unused input (a capture change),
 *  and DIOR/DIOW pick up the stretch terms.  Costs terms, not
 *  silicon - the reason this board owns its own strobe generation.
 *  Pin 23 and pin 1 are both free.
 *
 *  MEMRD_L / MEMWR_L / IOWIN_L are the PIN LEVELS of the active-low
 *  nets /MEMRD, /MEMWR, /IOWIN.  RST is active HIGH.
 *
 *  GATE: with RST low, the compiled JEDEC swept exhaustively against
 *  the map above (2^10 rows), then composed with IODEC_R16's over the
 *  full 2^18 address-and-strobe space: every strobe fires exactly on
 *  its documented addresses, the four held outputs never, nothing at
 *  or above 0x3FF0, nothing with A14 or A15 high - 0 mismatches.  With
 *  RST high, TMRACKWR asserts on every row and no other output differs
 *  from its RST-low value.  Checksum 5908, carried by
 *  R16_Peripheral.ttlproj and R16_4MHz_Board.ttlproj
 *  (Peripheral_Board.md).  BlinkyJED compile and parse-back is the
 *  ratifying gate; its output is the artefact of record.  Pin
 *  assignment matches R16_Peripheral.ttlproj.
 *
 *  Term counts: TMRSTARD, CS0, DIOR and DIOW one product term each,
 *  TMRACKWR two, the four held outputs none.
 */

/* ---- inputs, dedicated ---- */
/*  Pin 1 unused, tied to GND in the capture - see the stretch
 *  provision above before repurposing.  Pin 13 is J7's common: J7
 *  straps it to GND or to IORDY; no equation uses it yet.            */
PIN  2 = IOWIN_L;               /* /IOWIN from IODEC_R16 pin 21        */
PIN  3 = A0;
PIN  4 = A1;
PIN  5 = A2;
PIN  6 = A3;
PIN  7 = A4;
PIN  8 = A5;
PIN  9 = MEMRD_L;               /* /MEMRD pin level                    */
PIN 10 = MEMWR_L;               /* /MEMWR pin level                    */
PIN 11 = RST;                   /* active high, H7.2                   */

/* ---- outputs ---- */
/*  Pin 23 spare OLMC - the strobe-stretch reservation.                */
PIN 14 = !DIOW;                 /*  8 avail, 1 used - IDE 23           */
PIN 15 = !DIOR;                 /* 10 avail, 1 used - IDE 25, '245 DIR */
PIN 16 = !CS1;                  /* 12 avail, held - IDE 38, 10k PU     */
PIN 17 = !CS0;                  /* 14 avail, 1 used - IDE 37, 10k PU   */
PIN 18 = !TMRHIRD;              /* 16 avail, held - '590 U7/U8 /G      */
PIN 19 = !TMRLORD;              /* 16 avail, held - '590 U5/U6 /G      */
PIN 20 = !TMRCAPWR;             /* 14 avail, held - '590 x4 RCK        */
PIN 21 = !TMRACKWR;             /* 12 avail, 2 used - '74 /1CLR        */
PIN 22 = !TMRSTARD;             /* 10 avail, 1 used - '541 /G1         */

/* ================= common ================= */
IOWIN = !IOWIN_L;
RD    = !MEMRD_L;
WR    = !MEMWR_L;

/* ================= the tick, 0x3FC8 ================= */
TMRSTARD = IOWIN & !A5 & !A4 &  A3 & !A2 & !A1 & !A0 & RD;

/*  The acknowledge strobe doubles as TICKPEND's reset - see TICKPEND
 *  RESET in the header.  U9 pin 1 is its only consumer.              */
TMRACKWR = IOWIN & !A5 & !A4 &  A3 & !A2 & !A1 & !A0 & WR
         # RST;

/* ================= CF task file, 0x3FD0-0x3FD7 ================= */
CS0  = IOWIN & !A5 &  A4 & !A3;
DIOR = IOWIN & !A5 &  A4 & !A3 & RD;
DIOW = IOWIN & !A5 &  A4 & !A3 & WR;

/* ================= held high - see HELD OUTPUTS ================= */
TMRCAPWR = GND;
TMRLORD  = GND;
TMRHIRD  = GND;
CS1      = GND;
